{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqei61i2g5r","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Bucket cancelLegacySiblings match is too broad: catches implementation tasks mentioning daemon restart","summary":"The daemon-restart bucket's cancelLegacySiblings function (lib/followup-buckets.js:81) cancels any followup/* task whose title+prompt matches /restart.*daemon|daemon.*restart/i. This regex fires on IMPLEMENTATION tasks about the restart mechanism (e.g. \"fix acknowledgeDaemonRestartOnBoot\"), not just operational restart requests. Both gate-node implementation tasks were immediately canceled on creation because their prompts mentioned \"daemon\" and \"restart\".\\n\\nFix: the match predicate should require disruptive:true AND check metadata.follow_up_bucket, or narrow the regex to operational phrasing only (e.g. require the imperative verb \"restart\" at the start of the title). Implementation tasks about restart code should not coalesce into the operational bucket.\\n\\nThis is a latent bug that also explains why the gate node implementation should use a gate_kind field (structural) rather than prose titles that pattern-match into operational buckets.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T00:56:32.282Z","vec":[-0.10662822425365448,-0.009443636983633041,0.06034168601036072,-0.05206509679555893,0.043043557554483414,-0.01499972864985466,-0.00884227268397808,0.010391565039753914,0.028832130134105682,0.045219749212265015,-0.009741104207932949,0.014923343434929848,-0.012529309839010239,-0.058860234916210175,-0.016687482595443726,0.03209015354514122,-0.028605975210666656,-0.01679757796227932,-0.10282409936189651,-0.08081253618001938,0.051512304693460464,0.0066825104877352715,0.018157677724957466,0.04397785663604736,-0.06904429197311401,-0.018235724419355392,-0.07732192426919937,0.014195742085576057,0.027740810066461563,-0.02502959594130516,0.00979691743850708,0.09818454831838608,-0.021622080355882645,-0.06709656119346619,0.0059495423920452595,0.166493430733